+
+## Example: Two Sum Problem
+
+### Round 4 Failure
+```
+SAMPLES: FAIL (sample_1.txt: expected '1 2', got '0 1')
+TINY: FAIL (seed 0, expected '1 2', got '0 1')
+MAX: PASS
+```
+
+### Round 5 Diagnosis
+```
+Root Cause: Output uses 0-indexed instead of 1-indexed
+Fix: Add 1 to all returned indices
+Also: Replace O(N²) with O(N) hash map solution
+```
+
+### Round 5 Fix
+```python
+# BEFORE
+def two_sum(target, nums):
+    for i in range(len(nums)):
+        for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):
+            if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:
+                return (i, j)  # ❌ 0-indexed
+
+# AFTER
+def two_sum(target, nums):
+    seen = {}
+    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
+        complement = target - num
+        if complement in seen:
+            return (seen[complement] + 1, i + 1)  # ✅ 1-indexed
+        seen[num] = i
+```
+
+### Round 5 Verification
+```
+SAMPLES: PASS ✅
+RANDOM: PASS ✅
+MAX: PASS (0.01s) ✅
+Stress Test: ALL PASSED ✅
+```
+
+**Result**: Solution ready for production ✅
+
+---
+
+## Tools Available in Round 5
+
+### 1. verify_solution
+Quick verification with all gates:
+```python
+from tools.verify_solution import tool_function
+
